      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n\n## Column Mapping\n- academic years: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- academic year's description: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\n- standard deviation of enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- subjects: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- subject title: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- number of enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- fall term: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM\n- Mathematics department: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"math\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each academic year, what is the academic year description and the standard deviation of the number of enrolled students in library subjects offered during terms in that year, considering only years with more than 5 subjects offered, and only including subjects that are offered in the fall term and are from the Mathematics department (Course 18)?\n```sql\nSELECT ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, STDDEV(lso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS stddev_num_enrolled_students FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED lso JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL ata ON lso.TERM_CODE = ata.TERM_CODE JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ccso ON lso.TERM_CODE = ccso.TERM_CODE AND lso.SUBJECT_ID = ccso.SUBJECT_ID WHERE ccso.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND ccso.IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM = 'Y' GROUP BY ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC HAVING COUNT(*) > 5 ;\n```\n\n## Question\nFrom the top 10 academic years with the highest standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of enrolled students in library subjects offered during terms in that year (considering only years with more than 5 subjects offered, and only including subjects that are offered in the fall term and are from the Mathematics department), display each academic year's description, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of enrolled students, and the subject with the highest enrollment in that year, along with its subject title and number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers."
