enrollment-subject precedents: 1 (dw_4812, ROW_NUMBER pattern).\n\n## 4. Business Usage\n\nLIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED is consumed by 28 metrics for library-reserve enrollment analysis (dw_3393, dw_4584, dw_4724, dw_1301, dw_4812 …), typically joined to term dimensions for year attributes and to catalog/TIP tables for subject attributes. COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED is the canonical source for IS_OFFERED_* flags and DEPARTMENT_NAME filtering. ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL is the standard year/description enrichment table.\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED: semantic_get ✓, query_neighbors ✓, metrics_by_table ✓\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL: semantic_get ✓, concept membership ✓ (via concept_academic_term_dimension)\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: semantic_get ✓, concept comparisons ✓\n- dw_1301, dw_4812: semantic_get (full SQL) ✓\n- concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_academic_term_dimension: semantic_get ✓\n- Remaining Phase 1 entities (other offering tables, catalog feeds, column concepts): screened via concept comparisons/decision guides above; none carries both the library enrollment measure and the fall-term flag.\n- mysql_query verification: attempted 3× — all failed with `1045 Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'` (environment credential issue, not a SQL issue).\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Use LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED (SUBJECT_ID, SUBJECT_TITLE, NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (TERM_CODE → ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC) and COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (TERM_CODE + SUBJECT_ID; DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics', IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM='Y').\n\n**6b.** Build one `base` CTE with the exact dw_1301 join/filter; aggregate per year with `STDDEV()` and `HAVING COUNT(*) > 5`; pick the top-enrollment subject per year with `ROW_NUMBER() … ORDER BY NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS DESC` (dw_4812 pattern); order by stddev DESC and LIMIT 10. Caveat: catalog fan-out (multiple section rows per subject/term) is intentionally kept because the gold precedent dw_1301 computes STDDEV and COUNT(*) over the same joined row population.\n\n**6c.** Data perspective: only LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED has library-scope NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS; only COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED has IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM. Semantic-network perspective: documented joins (query_neighbors) and the concept decision guide for ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL confirm the join path. Business perspective: dw_1301 is an identical-shape precedent (same three tables, same filters, same HAVING), and dw_4812 establishes the highest-enrollment-subject ROW_NUMBER pattern.\n\n**6d.** No tie-breakers needed — evidence converges on a single candidate set.\n\nFinal SQL (SELECT list exactly: year description, stddev, subject id, subject title, enrolled students):\n\n",
